@style(../styles/IDocDemo.style)
@title(Theorems and proofs)

Numbered theorem-like blocks and proofs, and new kinds of your own.

@section(Theorem blocks)

@subsection(@@theorem)

A numbered theorem block (the family: lemma, proof, definition, corollary, example, note, proposition, remark).

@theorem(Sum of odd numbers) For every natural number n, @eqi(sum_{i=0}^{n-1} (2i+1) = n^2).
@end

@theorem(Square of a sum) For all natural numbers a and b, @eqi((a+b)^2 = a^2 + 2ab + b^2).
@end

@theorem(Pythagoras)
a^2 + b^2 = c^2
@end

@subsection(@@lemma)

A numbered lemma block.

@lemma … @end

@subsection(@@corollary)

A numbered corollary block.

@corollary … @end

@subsection(@@proposition)

A numbered proposition block.

@proposition … @end
Kirchhoff's voltage law: @q(fn: 0, label=kvl)
as in @qref(kvl)
@img(circuit.svg, w=120, label=fig1, alt=A circuit)
see @ref(fig1)

@subsection(@@definition)

A numbered definition block.

@definition(Entropy) … @end

@subsection(@@example)

A numbered example block.

@example … @end
call the @gloss(API)

@subsection(@@remark)

A numbered remark block.

@remark … @end

@subsection(@@proof)

A proof block (set in italics, ends with ∎).

@proof … @end

@proof(check)
induction n
step: sum_{i=0}^{n} (2i+1) = sum_{i=0}^{n-1} (2i+1) + (2n+1)   by sum
                           = n^2 + (2n+1)                        by IH
                           = (n+1)^2                             by ring
@end

@proof(check)
(a+b)^2 = (a+b)(a+b)        by ring
        = a^2 + 2ab + b^2   by ring
@end

@proof(goal="The sum of two even numbers is even")
Write 2a + 2b = 2(a + b).
@end

@subsection(@@newthm)

A theorem-like block of your own — newthm(conjecture, Conjecture) then conjecture … end.

@newthm(conjecture, Conjecture)

@newthm(claim, Claim, style=definition, counter=theorem)
